From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 12:00:00
Subject: [PATCH] guarded window geometry changes across a screen change

QWindow::setGeometry() resolves the screen the new geometry lands on and,
for a top-level window, calls QWindowPrivate::setTopLevelScreen() before
handing the geometry to the platform window. That emits screenChanged()
synchronously, and the application code it runs is free to destroy() the
window or to delete it outright; either way platformWindow is null when
setGeometry() then calls through it without re-checking.

The Windows screen removal path is what reaches this:
QWindowsScreenManager::removeScreen() moves every visible WS_EX_TOOLWINDOW
top-level window (tool panels, tooltips, popups) that lived on the
disconnected screen to the primary screen through setGeometry(), and
delivers a synchronous screen change for the rest. Both run the handlers
described above between iterations over a raw pointer snapshot of
QGuiApplication::topLevelWindows(), so later entries in the snapshot can
already be freed as well.

This was seen live on Windows: a tool window being moved off a
disconnected monitor crashed reading through the null platform window
right after the screenChanged() emission.

diff --git a/src/plugins/platforms/windows/qwindowsscreen.cpp b/src/plugins/platforms/windows/qwindowsscreen.cpp
index acbc93acfd3..9ed69cffd7d 100644
--- a/src/plugins/platforms/windows/qwindowsscreen.cpp
+++ b/src/plugins/platforms/windows/qwindowsscreen.cpp
@@ -13,6 +13,7 @@
 #include <QtCore/qt_windows.h>
 
 #include <QtCore/qsettings.h>
+#include <QtCore/qpointer.h>
 #include <QtGui/qpixmap.h>
 #include <QtGui/qguiapplication.h>
 #include <qpa/qwindowsysteminterface.h>
@@ -810,8 +811,21 @@ void QWindowsScreenManager::removeScreen(int index)
     // move those manually.
     if (screen != primaryScreen) {
         unsigned movedWindowCount = 0;
+        // Patched: both branches below run application code synchronously
+        // (screenChanged() handlers, the synchronous screen change delivery),
+        // and that code can delete windows still waiting in this snapshot.
+        // Hold them through QPointer and re-check each one before it is
+        // dereferenced, the way the leftover window loop on the screen
+        // removal path already does.
         const QWindowList tlws = QGuiApplication::topLevelWindows();
-        for (QWindow *w : tlws) {
+        QList<QPointer<QWindow>> windows;
+        windows.reserve(tlws.size());
+        for (QWindow *w : tlws)
+            windows.append(w);
+        for (const QPointer<QWindow> &guard : windows) {
+            QWindow *w = guard.data();
+            if (!w)
+                continue;
             if (w->screen() == screen && w->handle()) {
                 if (w->isVisible() && w->windowState() != Qt::WindowMinimized
                     && (QWindowsWindow::baseWindowOf(w)->exStyle() & WS_EX_TOOLWINDOW)) {
